NEON I2_S kernels: ggml_vec_dot_i2_i8_s and ggml_gemm_i2_i8_s

On ARM the I2_S mat-mul ran the scalar fallback. These follow the AVX2 kernels: a 128-element block is
two 16-byte halves of four 2-bit planes, the codes 0-2 are multiplied with the int8 activations through
ggml_vdotq_s32 (sdot with DOTPROD, vmull otherwise), the result is sum(code * y) and the n % 128 tail is
added with ggml_i2s_tail_dot. gemm uses 4x4 tiles of 16 int32x4 accumulators; leftover rows and columns
go through vec_dot. gemv already calls vec_dot.

